MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_001: Ahh, that smell! Perfect. It all comes down to\nusing fresh, quality leaves.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_002: I can also give myself credit for remembering the\nbrewing method. Delicious...
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_003: What is that scent? Seems like it's coming from\nright over... Oh! Gaitz!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_004: Ludia? Something wrong?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_005: What's that you're drinking? Tea?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_006: I have a talent for detecting where a tea is from,\nusually just from the smell of the leaves.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_007: That isn't a variety our company sells, so it must not\nbe anything grown in Dagda or Fódlan. Am I right?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_008: Hm, impressive! You're right. This is from the land\nof Sai, far to the east.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_009: All the way from Sai? How did you get it?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_010: Well, I have some connections in the country. I went\non my knight errantry there.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_011: I found this brew, and it was so delicious, I had to\nlearn how to make it.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_012: Would you like me to mix a cup for you? Unique,\nbut it might be to your liking.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_013: Are you sure? I'd love to try it!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_014: Huh... The way you brew it is completely different\nfrom how I've ever seen it done! You stir it?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_015: Yes. And while you do, you have to take care not to\nmake it foamy.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_016: Making tea is like an art on the frontier of Sai.\nThey call it "preserving the leaves' spirit."
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_017: Interesting... You seem to know a lot about eastern\ncultures, Gaitz... Wait. Now that I think about it...
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_018: Hm? What is it?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_019: My father has spoken of a Brezarant general\nnamed Gaitz.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_020: So...you're General Senghor's daughter?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_021: I am! And he said this other Gaitz knew martial arts\nfrom the east, which is why I just remembered...
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_022: Ah, it's a common enough name. And there are so\nmany who go on knight errantry.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_023: That's true! I'll have to ask Father about this other\nGaitz next time.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_024: Right. Ah, well. Still want a cup?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_025: Yes, please. Thank you so much! ...Yah! Bitter!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_026: Oh, sorry! {SetColor=Gray}I must've gotten distracted when she said\nthat about her father...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_027: It's still delicious though! I wouldn't say the bitterness\nis overpowering... I like it, actually!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_C_028: As long as you enjoy it...
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_001: General Gaitz! I'd like to ask about the formations\nused in the last battle. Can you spare a moment?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_002: Yes, alright. The intent was to draw the enemy in.\nSo, we positioned forces there and there...
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_003: I see! We were able to use their numerical\nadvantage against them!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_004: I shouldn't be surprised that General Senghor's\ndaughter has such a strong grasp of strategy.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_005: You're well on your way to being a great general.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_006: You're too kind... Hehehe. But who can say what the\nfuture holds?
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_007: I still know hardly anything about the east, so I have\na lot to learn before I can hold a candle to you!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_008: Well, that I can teach you. Starting with...how their\ntea is meant to taste.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_009: The brew I made you before was utterly botched,\nI'm sorry to say.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_010: It was?! But it tasted so good!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_011: It may have suited your palate, but it was not\nauthentic. I far oversteeped it.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_012: I was nervous you were closing in on my identity.\nNow that it's in the open, that won't be a problem.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_013: I can hardly wait! This'll be good!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_014: Alright, here you are. Tea as it's made in the land\nof Sai.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_015: Hmm. Let me try a sip... O-oh my!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_016: Hahaha! I know! Wonderful, isn't it? I'm sure it's a\ntreat for a connoisseur like you.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_017: I liked the last one a lot more! This feels somehow\nlacking in comparison.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_018: What? No, that was wrong. That wasn't how it was\nsupposed to taste.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_019: I suppose everyone has their own preferences.\nBut it's meant to be subtle in flavor.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_020: It's still good! I hope you're not disappointed.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_021: You made it just for me, and it's nothing like any tea\nI've had before. That's enough for me!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_022: That's...all very well, I suppose. I just wanted to make\nyou the authentic article.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_023: Don't worry so much! And more importantly, put\nsome more of that tea on to overbrew please!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_024: Ehe. Now we're talkin'! Mm!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_025: Gods. This feels like such an insult to the tea.
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_026: Hey! What'd you serve me this time, Gaitz?! This is\ncompletely different from the last time!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_027: Well, you try making a mistake the same way twice!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_028: What?! I can't believe this... I guess we'll just have\nto figure it out, step by step! That tea was perfect!
MID_SE_Gat_Lou_B_029: Perfectly wrong, you mean? I'm sorry, spirit of\nthe leaves.